## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to combine nonlinear PCA with streaming data, GPU acceleration, and production latency constraints in a high-throughput setting.

## Key Concepts
- Kernel PCA via random Fourier features
- Incremental SVD in RKHS
- Streaming imputation and normalization
- Drift detection and adaptive component retention
- Translating loadings into governance alerts under latency pressure

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo streaming kernel-PCA core
function processBatch(batch){
  const Z = mapToRF(batch.features); // random Fourier features
  const upd = incrementalSVD(Z, batch.mask);
  const comps = computeLoadings(upd);
  if (driftDetected(comps)) updateComponentPolicy();
  emitAlertsFromLoadings(comps);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate RK feature approximation quality in production?
- How would you handle non-stationary drift with changing feature distributions?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design edge-optimized streaming PCA with strict resource limits and actionable, interpretable alerts.

## Key Concepts

- Streaming PCA with randomized SVD
- Incremental imputation for missing data
- Drift detection on loadings for nonstationarity
- On-device latency/memory budgeting
- Interpretability of loadings for governance alerts

## Code Example

```javascript
// pseudo-code: streaming PCA update
function streamPCAStep(row, state) {
  const imputed = impute(row, state.imputer);
  const projected = project(imputed, state.components);
  state = updateSVD(state, projected);
  return state;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate drift thresholds in production?
- How would you balance on-device explainability with privacy constraints?

Why This Is Asked
Assesses edge deployment thinking: PCA under tight latency, memory, and drift, plus concrete handling of missing data and scaling.

Key Concepts
- On-device PCA projection and memory constraints
- Simple imputation and feature scaling in embedded environments
- Component retention criteria (variance explained, elbow)
- Drift monitoring and offline/online update strategies

Code Example
```javascript
// x: length-16 feature vector
// W: 4x16 projection matrix stored on device
function project(x, W){
  const y = new Array(4).fill(0);
  for(let i=0;i<4;i++){
    let s=0;
    for(let j=0;j<16;j++) s += W[i][j]*x[j];
    y[i] = s;
  }
  return y;
}
```

